{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 34, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 film directed by david fincher and written by grant heslov, benj pasek, and jared leto. the movie is a biographical drama based on the founding of mark zuckerberg and facebook.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jessie einstein, a shy and socially awkward college student who creates a website called \" Facemash\" that allows students to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also gets zuckerberg into trouble with the university administration.\n\nafter \"facemash\" is shut down, zuckerberg creates a new website called \"thefacebook\", which is initially intended for harvard students only. the site quickly gains popularity, and zuckerberg meets edward sutherland, a fellow student who becomes his roommate and business partner.\n\nas \"thefacebook\" grows in popularity, it attracts the attention of the wadsworth brothers, andrew and dylan, who drop out of college to pursue the site full-time. the brothers have a falling out with zuckerberg, and he is forced to turn to other investors to help him grow the site.\n\nmeanwhile, the film also explores the personal struggles of the characters, including the conflicts between zuckerberg and his best friend and college roommate, divya Narendra, played by ariane labed. the film also delves into the relationships between the characters, including the romance between zuckerberg and cambria mead, played by daisy dukes.\n\nthe film received widespread critical acclaim, with many praising the performances of the cast, particularly jessie einstein, who brought a nuanced and convincing portrayal of zuckerberg to the screen. the film's direction, cinematography, and editing were also widely praised, with many noting the film's dark and moody tone, which added to the overall sense of tension and drama.\n